# KNOWN GAP (found R47 Track D1 while auditing the receiver-kind axis of the
# primitive-receiver reject).
#
# The NOMINAL-RECEIVER cell of the "name list answers without checking the
# receiver" family. `to_lower` is a String method; a `Vector[String]` does not
# have it.
#
#   RUST gg   : REJECTS — `error[E_NoMethodFound]: no method `to_lower` found on
#               type `Vector[String]``. This is the correct behaviour.
#   SELF-HOST : ACCEPTS, then CC-FAILs — `incompatible types when assigning to
#               type 'Str' from type 'int'`, the same wrong mint the primitive
#               cells produced: a `Str` destination minted from the method NAME.
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS IS NOT PART OF R47 TRACK D1'S REJECT, and the reason is structural
# rather than a scope cut. Rust rejects the two receiver kinds from TWO
# DIFFERENT BRANCHES of the EMethodCall arm with different machinery:
#   - `base_name is None` (a PRIMITIVE receiver) — a small fixed method table
#     per primitive. That is the branch Track D1 mirrored, as
#     `typecheck.gg::reject_no_method_on_primitive`.
#   - `base_name.is_some()` (a NOMINAL receiver) — `has_inherent_only_impls`,
#     plus the D36 auto-deref rules for Guard / ReadGuard / WriteGuard / Box
#     wrappers and the NonDerefContainer rejects.
# The second needs the full builtin method table for every collection AND the
# wrapper/auto-deref decision procedure, neither of which the self-host has. It
# is a different fix, not another site of the same one.
#
# The typing half is one edit — withhold the String-returning ladder arm when
# the receiver resolves to `RTDefined`/`RTGeneric` — but it was NOT landed
# unmeasured: `join` alone belongs to three receivers in the Rust oracle
# (String, `Thread[T]` → T, `TaskGroup` → void), so withholding it needs the
# TaskGroup arm too, and `tests/fixtures/async_task_group.gg:8` calls
# `group.join()` on the bootstrap-adjacent corpus. Measure before landing.
#
# CORRECT behaviour: `gg check` REJECTS this program on every lane.
void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("A")
    print(v.to_lower())
